{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1251917-dev-blog-solar-bonds","id":1251917,"title":"[Dev Blog] Solar Bonds","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-09-06T08:10:45-07:00","id":1251917,"title":"[Dev Blog] Solar Bonds","content":"<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/solar-bonds-exalted-3rd-edition/\" target=\"_blank\">In which Vance and Minton talk a bit about the Solar Bond, and reveal some Lunar Charms which make use of it.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T08:42:22-07:00","id":1251921,"title":"","content":"The cause of Silver Pact and the Solar-Lunar war are intreasting to me (...I read it as MRL as the general). I also think it's intreasting that the Silver Pact isn't something from the time of Tumult, but rather dates back to the First Age to begin with.<br /> Oh, and the charms are cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T09:01:39-07:00","id":1251923,"title":"","content":"There's nothing wrong with the war, although I find it a bit obvious. It might be conceited, but I kind of prefer my own idea that the conflict was about the status of the Caul.<br /> <br /> A lot of the Charms are neat, though. After Charms for the Sworn Kinship, I probably should have expected a bunch of things in which the Solar Bond was a nice addition, rather than the single or sole focus. It surely makes sense to not have a bunch of Charms that are functionally useless if a player opts out of having a mate.<br /> <br /> I can also see the sense in not making it an entirely new Merit when a pre-existing one can already serve the desired function, in addition to general distribution through the Charms. And I find something intriguing in the modification to the Intimacy, as something that can potentially be in flux rather than being completely immutable.<br /> <br /> I like the way that they've used some of the fiction as a basis for some of those Charms, such as Lilith's story for the Perception Charm to instantly sense the reincarnation of your Mate.<br /> <br /> And I've reached a point in Xenoblade Chronicles 2 that makes the image of sharing use of an Artifact especially compelling to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T09:26:57-07:00","id":1251928,"title":"","content":"I've got this image of a solar and lunar repeatedly bouncing an Infinite Chakram off something so that the other catches it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T10:17:26-07:00","id":1251944,"title":"","content":"There should be a way for a lunar to bond with other beings if only temporarily. Locking them out of bond charms seems unfair unless bonds have a really negative effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T10:29:28-07:00","id":1251949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1251917-dev-blog-solar-bonds?p=1251944#post1251944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There should be a way for a lunar to bond with other beings if only temporarily. Locking them out of bond charms seems unfair unless bonds have a really negative effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you mean?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T10:48:47-07:00","id":1251951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1251917-dev-blog-solar-bonds?p=1251944#post1251944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There should be a way for a lunar to bond with other beings if only temporarily. Locking them out of bond charms seems unfair unless bonds have a really negative effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel as though you haven't read the Charms.<br /> <br /> Or... any of the preview...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T11:02:18-07:00","id":1251954,"title":"","content":"Hm. I like the idea of a Lunar who does NOT have a Solar Mate being able to do a solemn and sacred and sorcerous wedding ceremony the same way the original Bondmates did, thus gaining a Solar Mate in play. This might not be a charm, though, this seems like a sacred ritual ceremony, and therefore ideal Working territory.<br /> <br /> I would probably let a Lunar PC who wanted to do so do such a ceremony to seal an eternal alliance with a non-Solar and give them the same benefits. <br /> <br /> Either way, though it'd be a major story beat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T11:12:45-07:00","id":1251956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1251917-dev-blog-solar-bonds?p=1251954#post1251954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> therefore ideal Working territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would find that to be ideal Working territory in the same way that revitalising the progenitive Essence of a Dragon Blood is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T11:14:01-07:00","id":1251957,"title":"","content":"There's a couple of charms that have no benefit if you don't have a Solar Mate, I guess, but it seems to me to be a small enough number (I notice that one of these charms has another one as a prereq; the previous preview had no charms that were prereqs for others, which leads me to believe there's not much else in that tree) that I don't really mind.<br /> Most of them it's just an extra, and not enormous, benefit.<br /> <br /> If, like, 3% of charms are only usable for Lunars with Solar mates, that's fine. Just like if 10% of charms require a good Appearance and my character is ugly it's fine. Those just aren't charms I'll buy, but they fit someone else's concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T11:15:42-07:00","id":1251958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1251917-dev-blog-solar-bonds?p=1251949#post1251949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just that you are barred from a bunch of charms for not having a mate. Which, if you aren't near your mate is also useless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T11:33:10-07:00","id":1251962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1251917-dev-blog-solar-bonds?p=1251958#post1251958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just that you are barred from a bunch of charms for not having a mate. Which, if you aren't near your mate is also useless.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a Charm for making the Bond Tie inviolable, which is probably not the end of Lunar Intimacy protection Charms, and if you have no Mate... who cares?<br /> <br /> And, sure, being unable to share attunement of an Artifact, or instantly awaken Evocations when you make and gift it to somebody, is a loss, but it's just one thing.<br /> <br /> Every other damn Charm does things without needing to have your Mate around. A number of them use the Bond only in doing things <i>to</i> your Mate. Exactly who do you want to make lose points of Limit?<br /> <br /> And a couple of those enhanced effects seem far too powerful to access just by bonding yourself willy nilly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T11:35:06-07:00","id":1251963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1251917-dev-blog-solar-bonds?p=1251957#post1251957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just like if 10% of charms require a good Appearance and my character is ugly it's fine. Those just aren't charms I'll buy, but they fit someone else's concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>Person, that's what the Hideous Merit is for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T11:49:26-07:00","id":1251965,"title":"","content":"Not hideous, just ugly. Or plain.<br /> <br /> My point is that not every concept needs to take every charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T12:28:52-07:00","id":1251976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1251917-dev-blog-solar-bonds?p=1251958#post1251958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just that you are barred from a bunch of charms for not having a mate. Which, if you aren't near your mate is also useless.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s only unfair if the player doesn\u2019t have a choice about having a bond or not and what Charms to take. If having a Bond doesn\u2019t fit your concept you invest in different Charms and are not disadvantaged.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T12:32:28-07:00","id":1251977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1251917-dev-blog-solar-bonds?p=1251965#post1251965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not hideous, just ugly</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah; like the difference between somebody being tall, and having long body proportions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or plain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't the Attribute describe itself as being largely about posture and confidence, anyway?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point is that not every concept needs to take every charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think those are really the same, but it also doesn't matter because Epimetheus is not describing the Charms accurately.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T12:34:41-07:00","id":1251978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1251917-dev-blog-solar-bonds?p=1251976#post1251976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If having a Bond doesn\u2019t fit your concept you invest in different Charms and are not disadvantaged.</div> </div> </div> </div>Charm, singular.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T13:19:16-07:00","id":1251990,"title":"","content":"I like the approach to the Bond in this edition, from what I've seen so far. When I play a Lunar with the Bond as a significant part of their character, I generally want them to be good at protecting and supporting their mate, and these Charms look like a good complement to that.<br /> <br /> A Solar mate as a rival or hated enemy seems like an interesting option to explore, too, and I'm glad some Charms can work well with that too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/157-phoenix_kensai","name":"Phoenix_Kensai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar157_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T13:40:16-07:00","id":1252000,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m now imagining a First Age Lunar with Omniscient Instinct Concentration who\u2019s Mate was one of the Solars who kept reincarnating. Feeling that senation of joy at the reincarnation quickly followed by the pain of their death, over and over, across the millennia... That seems like it might screw you up a bit.<br /> <br /> I could imagine the Lunar becoming numb to it, until they sense the reincarnation....and the Solar doesn\u2019t die. Not after a week. Not after a Month. And the Lunar goes to find them, protect them, keep them safe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T13:51:51-07:00","id":1252002,"title":"","content":"&quot;Man, we've got to figure out how to turn my mate back into a Solar.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Yeah, these Deathknights are really spooky, and maybe dangerous.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;It's not <i>that</i>. I kinda like the goth look. It's just I've got a really sweet starmetal artifact that I took off that Sidereal I killed, and Abyssals aren't resonant with anything but soulsteel.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T14:13:11-07:00","id":1252004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1251917-dev-blog-solar-bonds?p=1251978#post1251978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Charm, singular.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be clear, the preview shows off many charms which benefit from having a solar mate, but they are quite useful without one. There is no need to avoid them merely because having a Solar Mate doesn't fit your character concept.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T14:34:20-07:00","id":1252012,"title":"","content":"One of them only gets a boost if your solar mate is an eclipse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T15:01:25-07:00","id":1252022,"title":"","content":"Love it.<br /> <br /> Willing to tolerate Blood-and-Tears Elixir being Stamina. Intelligence will have its own Medicine Charms, apparently including Night\u2019s Mercy Panacea. Also, the Charm is good. <br /> <br /> There\u2019s no point for Divine Paramour Embrace to reference a persuade action when the target MUST consent without resistance for the effect to have any effect. <br /> <br /> I\u2019m concerned about how often one would be able or need to use Taboo-Enforcing Beast, but I love how the Lunar could use it as the king with their own face, or as the stolen or borrowed face of a king or their Solar Mate as the king. Also the Lunar could use it as the American bald eagle to affect an American. Would the Realm count dragons as their animal?<br /> <br /> I\u2019m hoping that sight/hearing cousins of History-Divining Scent exist.<br /> <br /> I love Moon-and-Sun Panoply, particularly the allowance that a Lunar might craft an artifact for her Solar Mate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T15:11:30-07:00","id":1252025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1251917-dev-blog-solar-bonds?p=1252022#post1252022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There\u2019s no point for Divine Paramour Embrace to reference a persuade action when the target MUST consent without resistance for the effect to have any effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say it helps to characterise the action, and would also matter if the person <i>does</i> apply their Resolve.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love Moon-and-Sun Panoply, particularly the allowance that a Lunar might craft an artifact for her Solar Mate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the Solar Charms to awaken Evocations primarily for giving a bit of heft if an Artifact should be gifted or loaned, and the idea of a Lunar doing so for their Solar carries a similar, if not stronger, image.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T15:22:16-07:00","id":1252028,"title":"","content":"Not entirely clear what happens if the solar de-commits their attunement motes though. Does the lunar's attunement remain? Does the solar's? (It says it protects againt <i>any</i> effect that would break attunement...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T15:54:39-07:00","id":1252036,"title":"","content":"Since obviously the Bonds originate through past Exalted action this edition, I\u2019m inclined to say there is a lost \u201csacred marriage\u201d ritual that can allow a Lunar without a Bond to form one.<br /> <br /> Lunar/Lunar bonds seem plausible, and potentially could open up new Charm concepts involving things like form library sharing.<br /> <br /> Lunar/Sidereal Bonds would probably work more or less like Solar Bonds with some tweaked clauses on when certain Bonds apply (\u201ca society your Mate actively guides the rulers of\u201d rather than \u201ca society your Mate rules\u201d, etc).<br /> <br /> A Dragon-Blooded Bond could be interesting because instead of your Mate reincarnating, the Bond is passed to heirs down a family line (only one heir at a time though without heavy new charm design for charms that play off whole hosts of Dragon Blooded and are balanced accordingly).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T16:03:13-07:00","id":1252039,"title":"","content":"My personal preference is for the bond, and magics that tie into it, to be the emergent result of thousands of years of emotional connection, and not something you can duplicate with a spell or working without at least a thousand years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T16:09:47-07:00","id":1252042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1251917-dev-blog-solar-bonds?p=1252025#post1252025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd say it helps to characterise the action, and would also matter if the person <i>does</i> apply their Resolve.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Charm explicitly only works if they don\u2019t apply their Resolve. If the attempt is resisted and the Lunar seduces them anyway, the Charm does nothing.<br /> <br /> You might as well include unresisted social attempts for Solar Medicine Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T16:35:50-07:00","id":1252047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1251917-dev-blog-solar-bonds?p=1252042#post1252042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Charm explicitly only works if they don\u2019t apply their Resolve. If the attempt is resisted and the Lunar seduces them anyway, the Charm does nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I'm saying is that if the other party doesn't play along, it still functions as a normal persuasion action, that will require a Decision Point if it overcomes Resolve, just that it has a lot of wasted motes attached to it.<br /> <br /> Mostly though, I just think that it's described as being so because that's what seduction actions are. I don't think it detracts from the Charm in any way for it to be using terminology in a manner other than the strict mechanical interactions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might as well include unresisted social attempts for Solar Medicine Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>That... doesn't really track...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My personal preference is for the bond, and magics that tie into it, to be the emergent result of thousands of years of emotional connection, and not something you can duplicate with a spell or working without at least a thousand years.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> I'm inclined to view it as a combination of intrinsic functions of their Exaltation (and thus beyond all lesser magics), the unique alchemy of the mythic circumstances, the resonance of Chosen of Sun and Moon's duality (and, underneath that, the imagery of Solar might being able to tame the heart and temper of Lunar wildness), smoothed along a bit by the divine miracle of the Last City. </span></span></span></div><br /> It's not something that can be replicated with paltry sorcery, and probably nothing of its like will ever come again. Not without an act of plot equal to the significance of the creation of the Exalted, or a Yozi escaping, or managing to get rid of the Great Curse.<br /> <br /> I would definitely think that the significance of the Bond is cheapened if people are just going to connect it with whomever they please, and that if it's going to empower them so, the decision to not have the baggage of a past life connection to a Solar carries a meaningful sacrifice. Despite what Chompy managed in Masters of Jade, they're not entitled to having their cake and eating it too.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T16:53:42-07:00","id":1252050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1251917-dev-blog-solar-bonds?p=1251923#post1251923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's nothing wrong with the war, although I find it a bit obvious. It might be conceited, but I kind of prefer my own idea that the conflict was about the status of the Caul.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm unhappy with previous Exalted material that portrays the First Age Dragon-Blooded as nothing more than subservient adjuncts to the Solar Exalted. In that context, I feel that taking the Dragon-Blooded/Lunar conflict over the Caul and turning that into a Solar/Lunar conflict over the Caul is a bad look.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":18}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T17:10:52-07:00","id":1252053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1251917-dev-blog-solar-bonds?p=1252050#post1252050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm unhappy with previous Exalted material that portrays the First Age Dragon-Blooded as nothing more than subservient adjuncts to the Solar Exalted. In that context, I feel that taking the Dragon-Blooded/Lunar conflict over the Caul and turning that into a Solar/Lunar conflict over the Caul is a bad look.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get that, but part of the image I'm developing of the backstory for the Caul is that, having been a place that was mutually sacred to the Lunars and Dragon Blooded, they were often staunch allies in its defence during the First Age. That would often have been against threats from the Wyld or that emerged from its own nature, but occasionally from Solars and Sidereals who found its existence threatening, regardless of whose side Gaia was on.<br /> <br /> I didn't really picture Dragon Blooded being strongly involved in an original conflict leading to the formation of the Silver Pact, since that seemed especially personal to the Lunars, but that would have hardly been the last time that the place came under threat.<br /> <br /> I formed all of this around the idea that there's a tragic irony to how the Lunar and Terrestrial Exalted are now fighting tooth and nail over control of the Caul. That a sufficiently old (or immersed in past life memory) Lunar might look out over Faxai, with its patrols of the Wyld Hunt, from a high place, and have a bit of melancholy from a sharp flash to a time in which those groups fought side by side in defence of the place.<br /> <br /> To be clear, it wasn't an idea of Solars trying to take control of the Caul because they could get anything out of it; it was about Solars wanting to destroy or purge the place because they found any remnant of something beatified by a Primordial to be too threatening, to which Lunars vehemently disagreed. I would at least find that to be sufficiently distinct from the modern conflict over the place, and throw its contemporary stakes into sharp relief.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T17:33:23-07:00","id":1252057,"title":"","content":"Personally, while I do think it should be possible to replace a bond or form one where you had none, doing so should be the realm of individual plot devices with plenty of emotional and dramatic weight behind them (and which may or may not involve the First Age Lore specialist recreating the original ritual) and the bondmate should definitely still always be a Solar or former Solar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T18:03:10-07:00","id":1252062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1251917-dev-blog-solar-bonds?p=1252050#post1252050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm unhappy with previous Exalted material that portrays the First Age Dragon-Blooded as nothing more than subservient adjuncts to the Solar Exalted. In that context, I feel that taking the Dragon-Blooded/Lunar conflict over the Caul and turning that into a Solar/Lunar conflict over the Caul is a bad look.</div> </div> </div> </div>That must suck considering the tendencies fans have of reducing their importance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T18:38:16-07:00","id":1252072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1251917-dev-blog-solar-bonds?p=1252047#post1252047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That... doesn't really track...</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure it does. You need to persuade people to let you treat them.<br /> <br /> Even if they wouldn't even consider resisting, you need to go through the mechanical motions of persuading them to let you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T18:55:38-07:00","id":1252075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1251917-dev-blog-solar-bonds?p=1252072#post1252072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure it does. You need to persuade people to let you treat them.<br /> <br /> Even if they wouldn't even consider resisting, you need to go through the mechanical motions of persuading them to let you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't understand what point you're trying to make with this comparison against a Charm that is social in every step of its process.<br /> <br /> This all seems like a very long way to go to pick apart whether or not a given magical social action is accurate to call itself persuasion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T20:28:02-07:00","id":1252100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1251917-dev-blog-solar-bonds?p=1252075#post1252075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't understand what point you're trying to make with this comparison against a Charm that is social in every step of its process.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, you've forced me to finally go looking up the name of that Solar Presence Charm: Empowering Shout.<br /> <br /> Notice how the Solar doesn't need to bother with an Inspire roll which the target has to choose not to resist. The just allows you to assume that the target is willing enough to be inspired that the Solar doesn't need to bother with the mechanical action.<br /> <br /> If this Lunar Charm needs to bother wasting wordcount with a persuasion action, then there are a few Solar and Dragon-Blooded Charms that need to change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T20:35:03-07:00","id":1252104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1251917-dev-blog-solar-bonds?p=1252039#post1252039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My personal preference is for the bond, and magics that tie into it, to be the emergent result of thousands of years of emotional connection, and not something you can duplicate with a spell or working without at least a thousand years.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, I absolutely love this. That's my instinctive take.<br /> <br /> But I also don't wanna tell my players that their love (or, heck, their hate, I guess) isn't as powerful or mythic just because they haven't interacted much in past lives and it hasn't fermented properly yet. The Bond exists to model star crossed lovers across lifetimes...but hey, this should be able to be the first one. You should be able to swear oaths together that will bind you for all time, that will echo down into history for all time, that will bind the two of you together even after death does you part.<br /> <br /> First Age Exalts got to have better toys and infrastructure and do a lotta things better than Exalts can do now...but I don't see why marriage oughta be one of those things.<br /> <br /> What legends will they tell of your love?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T00:51:59-07:00","id":1252141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1251917-dev-blog-solar-bonds?p=1252100#post1252100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If this Lunar Charm needs to bother wasting wordcount with a persuasion action, then there are a few Solar and Dragon-Blooded Charms that need to change.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whhhyyyyyyyyyyyy?!?!<br /> <br /> And I don't mean &quot;why should they be changed&quot;, I mean why be like this about the Charm?<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh I like everything about what it does and what it means, but I'll die on the hill of how it specifically words itself.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1251917-dev-blog-solar-bonds?p=1252104#post1252104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I also don't wanna tell my players that their love (or, heck, their hate, I guess) isn't as powerful or mythic just because they haven't interacted much in past lives and it hasn't fermented properly yet. The Bond exists to model star crossed lovers across lifetimes...but hey, this should be able to be the first one. You should be able to swear oaths together that will bind you for all time, that will echo down into history for all time, that will bind the two of you together even after death does you part.</div> </div> </div> </div>Should Dragon Blooded be able to become Sworn Kin with whomever?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T04:36:08-07:00","id":1252175,"title":"","content":"I like these charms. <br /> <br /> They feel emotive, mythic and primal. Very Lunar. A Lunar NPC who has these Charms is of great significance, especially.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T05:37:11-07:00","id":1252188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1251917-dev-blog-solar-bonds?p=1252141#post1252141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Whhhyyyyyyyyyyyy?!?!<br /> <br /> And I don't mean &amp;quot;why should they be changed&amp;quot;, I mean why be like this about the Charm?<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Oh I like everything about what it does and what it means, but I'll die on the hill of how it specifically words itself.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Because I\u2019m autistic, and you used bad logic to defend losing something you don\u2019t need instead of gaining something you should want, which is a conservation of Wordcount.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T05:41:35-07:00","id":1252189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1251917-dev-blog-solar-bonds?p=1252050#post1252050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm unhappy with previous Exalted material that portrays the First Age Dragon-Blooded as nothing more than subservient adjuncts to the Solar Exalted. In that context, I feel that taking the Dragon-Blooded/Lunar conflict over the Caul and turning that into a Solar/Lunar conflict over the Caul is a bad look.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, it puts too much focus on the Caul, which shrinks the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T06:21:28-07:00","id":1252193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1251917-dev-blog-solar-bonds?p=1252189#post1252189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, it puts too much focus on the Caul, which shrinks the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>At the moment, all we have about the Caul is that many Lunars find it worth fighting the Dragon Blooded over control of it.<br /> <br /> I'm proposing a single event in the backstory of the Silver Pact that would contribute to why it is worth that attention.<br /> <br /> The Realm is going to posit the Caul as widely regarded as the birthplace of the Terrestrial Exalted. If it's supposed to be about as sacred to the Lunars (as I'm drawing from the fact that the shrine cities can become aligned with them instead), I think it warrants a historical event. <br /> <br /> I'm not suggesting that the entire Lunars book revolve around the place, but it getting <i>something</i> to elaborate its importance to the Lunars seems like an appropriate level of attention.<br /> <br /> And I would maintain that there can be something compelling, that can add to its narrative in the Time of Tumult, to the idea that the Lunars and Terrestrials have had a number of occasions in which they've fought together in defence of the Caul against powers hostile to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T06:23:47-07:00","id":1252196,"title":"","content":"Nah, the Hearth is about all being of the same mythic bloodline such that any two Dragonblooded are kin. You meet a random outcaste, you know he's your cousin somehow. It's not about Found Family so much as Blood Family.<br /> <br /> The Bond is about evoking the mythic connections between the sun and the moon, sure. I would make my Lunar players Bonding with anyone new a major story beat, a ceremony that comes after some epic romantic arcs or archnemesis arcs or something and rule it as magically formalizes what is already growing there.<br /> <br /> I want to go on record as saying I am not necessarily saying this oughta be enshrined in Canon? Like, the Bond mechanic seems super easy to adapt to non-Solar bonds, and 3E is all about letting you do whatever you want at your own table.<br /> <br /> I and my whole gaming group are a bunch big queer and often Poly nerds. Setting bits about how these other people's relationships are inherently more metaphysically potent than the ones you have been building are gonna rub a few of them the wrong way, and so in my games it's probably gonna end up possible for a Chosen of Jupiter to have as many Lunar Mates as the planet has moons, and that's fine for my game but probably doesn't need to be the default.<br /> <br /> I love the new bond mechanics-they look like they do what the game wants them to, and they'll do what I want them to do pretty easily too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T07:13:34-07:00","id":1252208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m concerned about how often one would be able or need to use Taboo-Enforcing Beast, but I love how the Lunar could use it as the king with their own face, or as the stolen or borrowed face of a king or their Solar Mate as the king. Also the Lunar could use it as the American bald eagle to affect an American. Would the Realm count dragons as their animal?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's something you can use a lot if running a society, I've just been having a discussion with one of my friends about how Herd-Reinforcement Stance and Taboo-Enforcing Beast can be used.<br /> <br /> So, for example, our Casteless Lunar, Timid Silk Blossom, has a Defining Tie to the Cult of the Illuminated (I think).<br /> <br /> So, say she's hanging around on Hen Ling, the theocratic righteous bandit village that serves as the centre of the Cult's power in the South (Kether Rock got destroyed by a Raksha invasion).<br /> Whenever a mortal from Hen Ling tries to criticise a Shining One* in front of her, she can use this charm.<br /> Whenever a mortal from Hen Ling refuses to do what a Shining One* tells them in front of her, she can use this charm.<br /> Whenever anyone from Hen Ling tries to commit a crime (other than, you know, righteous banditing) in front of her, she can use this charm.<br /> Whenever she sees a local eating on a fast day, she can use this charm.<br /> If she's ambushed by local thugs who've been paid off by the Realm, she can use this charm.<br /> If she's ambushed by local thugs who just want to beat and rob her, she can use this charm (it's a custom to rob outsiders, righteously, but not locals).<br /> If anyone says &quot;I don't want to be a righteous bandit, can't we make peace with our traditional enemies instead?&quot; she can use this charm.<br /> <br /> *Though here Shining One is defined by the local customs, not by her or the Cult's leadership. So King Ses, snakeman leader of the Eastern Cult and supreme gang-boss, probably wouldn't count because he doesn't fit the locals' view of a Shining One.<br /> <br /> And, very importantly, it's reflexive. It would be okay but not great if it was supplemental (it's not that difficult to resist), but it's reflexive. You could use it when ambushers are using Join Battle.<br /> <br /> It's probably not very useful in a game where you travel around a ton though, because you probably don't have Major intimacies to the cultures you interact with.<br /> <br /> The Changing Moon in the other game I play can take the shape of Prince Meek of Sukhmet and the Emperor of the Southern Dynasty, but even if she's swanning around as the Emperor she can't actually use this charm at all because she doesn't have a Major intimacy to the culture of the Southern Dynasty, she only went there for a couple of months. My own Lunar had a Major intimacy to a particular province of his homeland of Medo, but on our adventures he only ever met one other guy from there, who was just a minor NPC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 09-07-2018, 10:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T09:19:05-07:00","id":1252236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1251917-dev-blog-solar-bonds?p=1252141#post1252141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should Dragon Blooded be able to become Sworn Kin with whomever?</div> </div> </div> </div>They can, as long as \u201cwhomever\u201d is also Dragon-Blooded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T09:43:36-07:00","id":1252250,"title":"","content":"Yeah, a Lunar equivalent would be becoming the Lunar Mate of any Solar.<br /> <br /> With Lunar/Solar mates, if the Lunar PC becomes best buddies with a Solar, they can't form a bond.<br /> In our game, there's a Lunar Changing Moon who's married and has kids with a Night Caste, and she told him that, of course, she's his Lunar Mate... but she's not, and she knows that.<br /> <br /> Which is problematic in some ways, but I think there's a certain importance to mythic tropes.<br /> <br /> I think my favoured approach these days* would be to let people start without a mate, then if their Lunar is a great friend/lover with a Solar (PC or NPC) they could come to the ST and say they want to be Solar/Lunar mates, and then I'd say &quot;well, your characters get on really well because they're actually reincarnations of a hundred lives of totally top bros/legendary romances, and you were Solar/Lunar mates all along.&quot;<br /> <br /> *I tried to do some stuff with Lunar mates in 2e, and I don't think it worked that well.<br /> <br /> But... that actually doesn't work with the current system, because Lunars immediately recognise their Solar mates as such.<br /> <br /> Though that is important for stuff like doomed love (&quot;I met this incredibly hot vampire, and he's so hot... but so evil! Oh, the angst!&quot;). Which is exactly why some people play Lunars with Solar mates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T10:38:28-07:00","id":1252270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1251917-dev-blog-solar-bonds?p=1252104#post1252104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Bond exists to model star crossed lovers across lifetimes...</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Star-crossed&quot; refers to something being doomed to <i>failure</i>. The idea is that the stars themselves are set against this romance happening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T10:39:33-07:00","id":1252271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1251917-dev-blog-solar-bonds?p=1252236#post1252236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They can, as long as \u201cwhomever\u201d is also Dragon-Blooded.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's an advantage there to be sure of being the Exalted that consists of tens of thousands of people, but it's still something deeply embedded in the mythic undertones of those Exalted, that they can't reapply at will or convenience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T10:43:41-07:00","id":1252275,"title":"","content":"Last I checked forming or joining a Hearth isn\u2019t something you can only ever do once.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T11:22:05-07:00","id":1252292,"title":"","content":"Thinking some more about Taboo-Enforcing Beast and its prereq, you could combine it well with Establishing Facts. Establish a fact that X is a cultural custom, and then use your charms to enforce it on those who don't obey that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T11:27:17-07:00","id":1252295,"title":"","content":"Anyway, Robert Vance explained that the extra wordcount and complication of Divine Paramour\u2019s Embrace is intentional. The Charm\u2019s effect is intended to sometimes serve as a REASON for the target to give into a persuasion action and round of physical Intimacy when otherwise they might consider resisting.<br /> <br /> So a Solar might know that sleeping with the Lunar would be giving up his face to her, but he might really need those Willpower points for an upcoming challenge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T11:28:56-07:00","id":1252296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1251917-dev-blog-solar-bonds?p=1252271#post1252271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's an advantage there to be sure of being the Exalted that consists of tens of thousands of people, but it's still something deeply embedded in the mythic undertones of those Exalted, that they can't reapply at will or convenience.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t recall seeing the mechanics for how a Hearth is formed. I assumed it was so easy that no mechanics were needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T11:51:23-07:00","id":1252300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1251917-dev-blog-solar-bonds?p=1252270#post1252270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Star-crossed&quot; refers to something being doomed to <i>failure</i>. The idea is that the stars themselves are set against this romance happening.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunar and Solar Bondmates are the archetypal star crossed lovers. Mythic love and mythic tragedy go hand in hand.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also there's literal agents of fate who probably are trying to kill both of you or keep you from getting together, so...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T11:53:58-07:00","id":1252302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1251917-dev-blog-solar-bonds?p=1252296#post1252296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t recall seeing the mechanics for how a Hearth is formed. I assumed it was so easy that no mechanics were needed.</div> </div> </div> </div>There\u2019s a specific ceremony involved but that\u2019s it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T13:14:27-07:00","id":1252327,"title":"","content":"So one thing I've been giving some thought to is the lunar bond from the solar perspective. WAIT!, don't mob me yet, hear me out!<br /> <br /> The Solar bond is being described in 3E as a part of a deal or negotiations that ended a war fairly decisively and was meant to help ensure it would never happen again. My take on the preview made it seem like there were Solars and lunars on both sides of the war but apparently the bond helped ease tensions and create a lasting peace.<br /> <br /> Cool.<br /> <br /> Now on one hand, we've got the lunars, shapeshifting piles of awesome who've got a bunch of charms that work as normal most of the time but if you've got your solar bond next to you, these charms work even better. On the other side of it, the Solars get... whatever bonus their lunar mate chooses to impart to them. This strikes me as odd. If the bond was conceived as part of a negotiation to support lasting peace, why is it entirely up to one side to decide what benefits they both get out of it?<br /> <br /> Then I thought: &quot;What if the concession the lunars demanded was that the bond be entirely on their terms?&quot; &quot;The Solars get wicked sweet bonuses from this stuff, but it's up to the lunar to make that happen. Permanently gives them something the Solars may want, but also gives the lunars all the leverage in any kind of negotiation. A solar pisses off their bond mate and not only does it all go away, it potentially gets really, really bad.<br /> <br /> If this was all decided in a big negotiation between solars and lunars, I feel like this implies that the lunars were <i>hella </i>persuasive to get this level of concession. Plus this actually does make sense to encourage long term peace as it gives the group that would normally be considered the underdogs in a pile-up (one-on-one anyway, I believe there's now more lunars than solars in 3E so it may well be the other way around), some really potent permanent leverage to even the odds at the same time. PLUS it also reinforces the Solar/Lunar team up power-level and makes it basically impossible for someone to use the old 'divide and conquer' trick on them, making the entire deliberative more stable and powerful as a result... just not y'know invulnerable... *cough* usurpation *cough*<br /> <br /> Just my thoughts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T13:49:29-07:00","id":1252336,"title":"","content":"While the Bond itself is not something inherent in Lunar Exaltation as in 2E, I think the fact that Lunars have the actual mechanics side of the Bond in their Charmset and Solars don\u2019t does reflect something about Lunar Exaltation vs Solar Exaltation, and how Lunars are given to metaphysically adapt to their circumstances and create new strengths through change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T13:57:37-07:00","id":1252337,"title":"","content":"A lot of the charms that benefit from the bond do so when used in ways that benefit the solar. You can enforce the taboos of a society the solar rules, reinforce an oath the solar sanctifies, get better range on an investigation charm in pursuit of one of the solar's intimacies...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-08T04:44:13-07:00","id":1252479,"title":"","content":"I think that what the Solars got was that the Lunars would accept the Solars as the (theoretically) undisputed God-Kings of Creation, and a bunch of Lunars who could assist them in being that. The fact that the Lunars benefit from Solars being around when they use these charms doesn't change that the Solars benefit a lot from a Lunar bond-mate who is on side so to speak. It promotes co-operation between them, which was kind of the point (and I like that this was something the Solars and Lunars decided on, not the Incarnae, who were probably pleased but weren't part of the plan).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-08T04:49:38-07:00","id":1252483,"title":"","content":"&quot;The solars and lunars did it&quot; is probably the most significant change to the bond this edition, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-08T08:26:44-07:00","id":1252510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1251917-dev-blog-solar-bonds?p=1252483#post1252483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;The solars and lunars did it&quot; is probably the most significant change to the bond this edition, really.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know which is the most significant chance, but that is definitely significant, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-08T12:35:32-07:00","id":1252576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1251917-dev-blog-solar-bonds?p=1252483#post1252483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;The solars and lunars did it&quot; is probably the most significant change to the bond this edition, really.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's kind of along the line of greater autonomy for Lunars in the game. They didn't have Bond put onto them by thier goddess, and they didn't have Castes breaking happen to them by the world. They were involved in the creation of both pretty clearly by their own volition and aciton, whcih is pretty neat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-08T14:01:20-07:00","id":1252597,"title":"","content":"Even apart from the clarification, the use of a persuade action in the Lunar charm and the lack of such in the Solar charm is not necessarily a defect on the part of the <i>Lunar</i> charm.<br /> <br /> I love 3e, it's got a solid core engine, and I like most of the charms in the corebook, but let's not pretend it doesn't have some awkwardness in there, either. Like most of Craft. But you have to balance many needs and the circumstances of the charms are such that it's reasonable to assume the Solar charm is not going to be meaningfully resisted (&quot;Oh no, how horrible, you're giving me more willpower to carry on!&quot;), whereas Lunars can do enough stuff with physical intimacy that the extra verbiage isn't wasted wordcount at all. You're just not seeing the full picture.<br /> <br /> If the Solar mate has to consider that accepting the seduction means the Lunar might be able to take their shape or do some wacky Intimacy-affecting magic or any number of things, then yes, spelling out &quot;this is a persuade action for physical intimacy, not necessarily sexual, and it only works if the target accept this&quot; is <i>actually rather important</i>. If anything I'd add wordcount so the final product - perhaps in the intro to the charms section if we have several charms of this nature - make it clear you don't need to have sex. A massage or cuddling or any number of things count, too, and that's something very important to have out there.<br /> <br /> (I like my &quot;Exxxalted&quot; moments fine and once played a Jadeborn to Essence 5 so she could have Appearance 10 via Alchemical charms just for the jokes. But I wouldn't force my sense of humor on anyone.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-08T16:15:29-07:00","id":1252621,"title":"","content":"Personally I feel most sorry for the groups who are going to see the \u201cat least a scene of\u201d and forget that \u201cYou sneak off somewhere to bang/cuddle/make out\u201d is a full scene on its own. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-08T18:05:25-07:00","id":1252635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aliasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1251917-dev-blog-solar-bonds?p=1252597#post1252597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even apart from the clarification, the use of a persuade action in the Lunar charm and the lack of such in the Solar charm is not necessarily a defect on the part of the <i>Lunar</i> charm.<br /> <br /> I love 3e, it's got a solid core engine, and I like most of the charms in the corebook, but let's not pretend it doesn't have some awkwardness in there, either. Like most of Craft. But you have to balance many needs and the circumstances of the charms are such that it's reasonable to assume the Solar charm is not going to be meaningfully resisted (&quot;Oh no, how horrible, you're giving me more willpower to carry on!&quot;), whereas Lunars can do enough stuff with physical intimacy that the extra verbiage isn't wasted wordcount at all. You're just not seeing the full picture.<br /> <br /> If the Solar mate has to consider that accepting the seduction means the Lunar might be able to take their shape or do some wacky Intimacy-affecting magic or any number of things, then yes, spelling out &quot;this is a persuade action for physical intimacy, not necessarily sexual, and it only works if the target accept this&quot; is <i>actually rather important</i>. If anything I'd add wordcount so the final product - perhaps in the intro to the charms section if we have several charms of this nature - make it clear you don't need to have sex. A massage or cuddling or any number of things count, too, and that's something very important to have out there.<br /> <br /> (I like my &quot;Exxxalted&quot; moments fine and once played a Jadeborn to Essence 5 so she could have Appearance 10 via Alchemical charms just for the jokes. But I wouldn't force my sense of humor on anyone.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Appearance got another dimension for 3e, though, so in the context of this edition, that character would have made a wonderful front-position leader for battle groups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-08T18:30:32-07:00","id":1252639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1251917-dev-blog-solar-bonds?p=1252483#post1252483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;The solars and lunars did it&amp;quot; is probably the most significant change to the bond this edition, really.</div> </div> </div> </div>A change in the mythology is nice, but I'd say that the most important practical change is that it shifts a lot of the power and agency to the Lunar, and has less of a direct drawback.<br /> <br /> I had not fully remembered the Solar Bond Background; I forget that it gave a reserve of bonus dice to be used in aid or defence of the Solar, in addition to the Mental Defence Value modifiers. On the face of it, that doesn't strictly lack versatility in how it's applied, so it isn't necessarily servile, but it does have the issue that the more power you have to call upon, the more is being ceded to the Solar. It didn't help that the Background's text focused primarily on things like level of devotion and the effect of loss; we're told about Lilith staying with Desus through terrible abuse, and not one word for the kinds of things that she might have used those ten extra dice for.<br /> <br /> Distribution through the Charms and detachment from the strength of the Intimacy (in most regards) shifts a good deal of the power to the Lunar's court. You get more emphasis on things like collaboration and partnership, if not the Solar actually being a means to the Lunar's ends. You get benefits that the Lunar can bestow upon the Solar at their own discretion, and that can sometimes consist of the Solar giving ground.<br /> <br /> The mythology strikes me as being a relatively minor extension of this changed dynamic. It's still quite good! But I think the most important change isn't about where it came from, but where it can go from here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-09T01:23:09-07:00","id":1252694,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I never remembered to use my Solar bond dice, my Solar mate never made social attacks on me, and the other character with Solar Bond 5 never used it either (partly because the player never remembers or uses stuff like pools of extra dice in any game, and partly because the guy playing her Solar mate dropped out after a few months). <br /> <br /> Mechanically, it looks much more interesting and varied this time. Though of course, still not much help if your Solar mate dies/goes far away/is incompetent/is a duck. But that's always the case with cooperative mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-09T09:50:40-07:00","id":1252784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1251917-dev-blog-solar-bonds?p=1252694#post1252694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though of course, still not much help if your Solar mate dies/goes far away/is incompetent/is a duck.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they'd better shape up...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-09T11:31:35-07:00","id":1252813,"title":"","content":"I meant to write &quot;is a dick.&quot; Typo.<br /> Because, if your Solar Mate has been turned into a duck, the extra dice to help her probably actually are quite useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-09T13:00:36-07:00","id":1252830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1251917-dev-blog-solar-bonds?p=1252813#post1252813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant to write &quot;is a dick.&quot; Typo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh, that's no fun.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-09T13:36:43-07:00","id":1252840,"title":"","content":"Mess with one duck, they gotta deal with the whole flock.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThe very existence of flame-throwers proves that some time, somewhere, someone said to themselves, You know, I want to set those people over there on fire, but I'm just not close enough to get the job done.\u201d George Carlin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/123-trax","name":"Trax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar123_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-09T13:46:56-07:00","id":1252842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1251917-dev-blog-solar-bonds?p=1252635#post1252635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Appearance got another dimension for 3e, though, so in the context of this edition, that character would have made a wonderful front-position leader for battle groups.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, technically it's just an elaboration of the dimension it already had. And the character in question, since Jadeborn shared relatively small essence pools with raksha, relied on the attribute augmentations in general so she also wound up with a very high <i>everything else</i>, between Artisan natively high stats and charm boosts. In the end I had her be a Supergirl-style inspiring superhuman figure who wasn't quite Solar awesome, so yes, that would have worked out.<br /> <br /> This is mildly relevant in that it's good to see Lunar Appearance is also getting a fair latitude adjustment, as opposed to 1e's &quot;we don't want to disadvantage ugly Lunars&quot;. Because 3e Appearance is more about initial impact and first impressions than anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}